Scripts examples

1. Prepare a valid SWAT 2012 project and identify HRU `.mgt` files.
2. Confirm the SWAT LUSE codes used in your project.
3. Prepare or select LUSE-specific management templates for Part A (see o mgt_LUSE.R).
4. Identify the eligible forestry-conversion HRUs using the baseline map (in this case the code is ESC).
5. Select the species-specific staggered-plantation routine (Pine or Eucalyptus).
6. Set project input/output folders and random seed.
7. Run the relevant pathway and write scenario-specific `.mgt` files to a separate output directory.
8. This files can then be substituted in one model folder to run the specific scenario. 
9. Compare original and modified schedules, checking operation counts, planting years, rotation sequences, and parameter values before running SWAT.
